From: dennitino <alanw6118@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] topaz-0954: net: log configd's ioctls on en0 too

After a WPA2 join asked by wifid the link is up and the keys are in, but no
frame is ever sent (no DHCP). Whether configd looks after en0 at all is the
question: its ioctls were left out of the log. Log its first 60, with the
interface's flags and the link state.

--- a/bsd/dev/redwood_net.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/redwood_net.c
@@ -198,6 +198,18 @@
 			printf("net: en0 is asked %#lx by %s\n", command, who);
 		}
 	}
+	if (net_link->wireless) {
+		/* topaz-0954: configd's too (whether it looks after en0 at all: DHCP starts there) */
+		static unsigned configd_said;
+		char who[32] = "?";
+
+		proc_selfname(who, sizeof(who));
+		if (strcmp(who, "configd") == 0 && configd_said < 60) {
+			configd_said++;
+			printf("net: en0 is asked %#lx by configd (flags %#x, link %s)\n", command,
+			    (unsigned)ifnet_flags(ifp), net_link_up ? "up" : "down");
+		}
+	}
 	switch (command) {
 	case SIOCSIFADDR:
 		ifnet_set_flags(ifp, IFF_UP, IFF_UP);
